{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics","id":1338477,"title":"Exalted 3E homebrew combat mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-29T10:33:04-07:00","id":1338477,"title":"Exalted 3E homebrew combat mechanics","content":"I'm looking for fan rewrites of 3E combat systems. I'm aware of Simon Darkstep's Momentum Exalted and Dragonmystic's Exalted : Reincarnated, but are there any others? I'll keep a list of them in this thread for easy access.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3E Homebrew combat systems :<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\">Momentum Exalted</a> - Simplifies initiative (renamed momentum) and uses a Battle Wheel to determine turn order.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1331162-wip-exalted-distilled-reincarnated\">Exalted : Reincarnated</a> - In-depth changes to the 3E core. Replaces initiative with Endurance, a secondary health pool that can regenerate. Work in Progress.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Glory Overwhelming</a> - Rework of the motes system. Exalts have near infinite motes, but frivolous spending ignites their Essence Fever, spurring them towards passionate and heroic action.<br /> <br /> Hissatsu - Rework of initiative. Creates risk/reward by making initiative your protection against decisive damage but also your fuel for Decisive Attacks and Gambits.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Hissatsu Differences</b><br /> <b>Initiative</b><br /> Initiative is no longer your damage potential, but functions more like a decisive soak. The higher your initiative, the less decisive damage you take. The more in the negatives you are, the more decisive damage you take. Initiative recharges automatically when you do not attack and when you crash enemies. Withering attacks no longer grant initiative.<br /> <b>Withering</b><br /> - Withering attack damage does not get threshold successes added and post-soak damage is applied straight without rolling. Withering attacks do not give Initiative from hitting or damage, only on crashing.<br /> - Withering attack is one roll, attacking party doesn\u2019t need to do damage math or alter their own Initiative.<br /> <b>Decisive</b><br /> - Decisive attacks use Accuracy too. Decisive raw damage is based on the attacker losing 1-20 Initiative to serve as the base pool, modified by the target\u2019s Initiative. Negative Initiative adds to damage, positive Initiative lowers it. Total decisive damage rolled is capped by Lethality based on the genre after Hardness check.<br /> - Initiative acts like Decisive soak, with negative Initiative increasing damage. Attempting to attack high Initiative targets makes attacker vulnerable.<br /> <b>Gambits</b><br /> - Gambit Initiative check is 100% tied to Commitment. Commit 1-20 Init, roll Commitment dice without double 10s against gambit difficulty, on success you are in a position to attempt it. If you fail, you weren\u2019t in position to attempt the gambit. If the Gambit targets an enemy, resolve decisive attack/social influence action. If the Gambit requires e.g. a feat of strength, resolve the check. On success, gambit happens.<br /> - Gambits are always available, but attempting them makes you vulnerable.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Edit : added Lumi's Glory Overwhelming and Hissatsu</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 10-02-2019, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T07:19:36-07:00","id":1338623,"title":"","content":"What is it that you don't like about 3E combat?<br /> <br /> Cause, you know, 1E, Power Combat, 2E and 2.5 all exist.<br /> <br /> Personally, I still like porting the Exalted setting to Wild Talents (better fidelity) or Mutants and Masterminds (better balance) and let the PCs innovate their custom superpowers based on the fluff of Exalted Charms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T07:42:07-07:00","id":1338627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338623#post1338623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it that you don't like about 3E combat?<br /> <br /> Cause, you know, 1E, Power Combat, 2E and 2.5 all exist.<br /> <br /> Personally, I still like porting the Exalted setting to Wild Talents (better fidelity) or Mutants and Masterminds (better balance) and let the PCs innovate their custom superpowers based on the fluff of Exalted Charms</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like 3E's combat, I'm looking to tweak it rather than change it completely.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for inspiration to homebrew my own combat rules, trying to see if I can improves some of the weird aspects such as :<br /> <br /> <br /> -farming ini on one target and unleashing it on another being an optimal strat in many cases<br /> <br /> -area attacks / ganging up on 1 person being extremely powerful by the nature of the system, meaning a full circle can defeat nearly any non-legendary size threat just by sheer initiative advantage and aoe enemies become exponentially stronger the more enemies they fight.<br /> <br /> -lots of cases where the system falls apart if players don't play along, and the only thing keeping things in check is the Core book saying &quot;plz don't do dis&quot; rather than actual rules and limits<br /> <br /> -the conservation of ninjutsu effect with battle groups, where a single blood ape is much more dangerous than a battle group of 20 blood apes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-30-2019, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T10:08:27-07:00","id":1338643,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know of any alternate systems but some of your problems might have some built in mitigation that you\u2019re not taking full advantage of?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338627#post1338627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-farming ini on one target and unleashing it on another being an optimal strat in many cases</div> </div> </div> </div>I THINK this exact reason is why Initiative Shift is so punishing. If you crash one foe and then decisive kill another you\u2019re sitting at 3 initiative with the guy you crashed unwounded, if he just deals 3 withering damage to you he\u2019ll get a ton of initiative and probably three turns in a row. That might not actually help you if some enemies in the combat are just so weak that they can\u2019t meaningfully hit anything, but if that\u2019s the case they should either be sidelined or treated as trivial opponents as per the page 208 sidebar. <br /> <br /> That doesn\u2019t really help you though if you just feel like I doesn\u2019t make sense to gain a ton of combat momentum off of one person and unleash it on another through system abstraction of narrative combat. One thing I\u2019ve seen as a quick fix is to just keep everything the same except treat damage like battlegroups. If an enemy is crashed then withering damage goes straight to their health track, so that might be a good place to start for your homebrew.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338627#post1338627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-area attacks / ganging up on 1 person being extremely powerful by the nature of the system, meaning a full circle can defeat nearly any non-legendary size threat just by sheer initiative advantage and aoe enemies become exponentially stronger the more enemies they fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit I don\u2019t really get this one. I think that a full circle of Solars really SHOULD kick all kinds of ass against one single enemy. That\u2019s balanced by the fact that most great enemies have the resources of several nations at their disposal. If your PCs reach Alhat to fight him with even half their resources unspent you may have terribly underestimated the power that a directional war god commands. <br /> <br /> Also AoE attacks are you referring to? Are we talking like Death of Obsidian Butterfies?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338627#post1338627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-lots of cases where the system falls apart if players don't play along, and the only thing keeping things in check is the Core book saying &quot;plz don't do dis&quot; rather than actual rules and limits</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain these further? Do you mean like not hitting allies to farm initiative off them?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338627#post1338627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-the conservation of ninjutsu effect with battle groups, where a single blood ape is much more dangerous than a battle group of 20 blood apes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think strictly speaking this is true. Twenty bloodapes are absolutely more deadly run as individuals than in a battlegroup, but I think they\u2019re more deadly than a single one for sure.<br /> <br /> A BG of 20 apes though is like one ape that can attack everything in short range, has 21 health levels healable with rally for numbers, 6 parry, 9 soak, an attack with 15 accuracy and 19 damage, can boost that with command rolls, and who doesn\u2019t give up more than 1 initiative to withering attacks unless they deplete a magnitude in which case they get 6.<br /> <br /> Also RAW if you have 4 initiative and a battlegroup deals 10 damage to you, the first 4 crash you and the next 6 deal decisive damage in the one attack.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not going to kill a whole circle on their own like 20 individual apes might, but paired with a commander like Sigereth or Octavian or an Exalted commander and they can do some serious damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T11:36:19-07:00","id":1338659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338627#post1338627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-lots of cases where the system falls apart if players don't play along, and the only thing keeping things in check is the Core book saying &amp;quot;plz don't do dis&amp;quot; rather than actual rules and limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sincerely hope you find what you're looking for. (Following the thread with interest.) But almost every subsystem over every single edition of Exalted relies on the ST and players putting effort into not breaking the system.<br /> <br /> I've never seen a robust set of houserules that addresses this -- but you're probably looking for complete rewrites like Exalted : Reincarnated.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think you should run Mutants and Masterminds. The system isn't impossible to break, but it's pretty difficult -- especially if you insist on every Power being modelled on a published Exalted Charm. M&amp;M solves all your issues apart from &quot;conservation of ninjutsu&quot; (which is <i>massively</i> exacerbated).<br /> <br /> Otherwise:<br /> <br /> 1. The only way of fixing this is to track Initative on every combatant for every combatant... which is massively math intensive. Momentum doesn't try to address it (and Reincarnated is a system rewrite to the scale of Dungeons the Dragonning). I guess the advice on page 194 of the Corebook <i>kinda</i> helps? (SHENANIGANS!) But you don't need homebrew to apply that.<br /> <br /> 2a. Area attacks typically only award Initative from one target. Where they don't, houserule they do to fix that. Simples.<br /> 2b. I'd be tempted to do something like FFG Edge of the Empire and give Boss characters two Initative tracks (a bit like how Single Point Form works). But this is kinda a feature of the system -- the Exalted (especially Solars) are the biggest bads in the setting. Each individual PC is a world shaping powerhouse, that Wyld Hunts want to gang up on at least 5-to-1. If the Circle gets a numerical advantage... well they're <i>supposed</i> to wipe the floor with their foes. No &quot;but what about&quot; -- the Exalted wrested Creation from the <i>nigh omnipotent beings from beyond reality who birthed dieties to serve them as slaves</i>. They're supposed to be able to kick the ass of <i>anything</i> in the setting, and to kick the ass of <i>most things</i> even when outnumberered.<br /> <br /> 3. &quot;plz don't do dis&quot; is basically the Storyteller's Guide for Exalted. It's practically the slogan of the gameline. You need to houserule and you need players who'll work with you.<br /> <br /> 4. If battlegroups are posing that much of an issue, then don't use them. Roll in 20 individual Blood Apes. Or once the battgroup is defeated, roll in a single survivor as an individual combatant. Or cheat the battlegroup's stats higher. Or don't use the combat system and run the encounter narratively. Use the advice on page 212.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:15:49-07:00","id":1338665,"title":"","content":"Oh one thing I\u2019ve done with battlegroups before, which I\u2019m not even sure isn\u2019t RAW, is to let them keep their charms. I don\u2019t see anywhere that battlegroups of one type of creature don\u2019t get to keep their charms, and a battlegroup of blood apes with Principle of Motion and Shattering Roar is fucking terrifying. As per ranged battlegroup attacks those roars are still AoE. Although still much less scary than 20 actual apes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Especially if they\u2019re commanded, since command rolls add to all actions taken that turn, so you blowout a command roll and have the apes attack twice with no flurry penalty and with like 25 dice each time.<br /> <br /> Double-edit: Actually my suggestion might not just be technically RAW but even intended so...yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-30-2019, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:28:23-07:00","id":1338669,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly a post in Ask the devs stated that Might is supposed to emule Charms, so that battlegroup do not use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:34:05-07:00","id":1338670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338627#post1338627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do like 3E's combat, I'm looking to tweak it rather than change it completely.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for inspiration to homebrew my own combat rules, trying to see if I can improves some of the weird aspects such as :<br /> <br /> <br /> -farming ini on one target and unleashing it on another being an optimal strat in many cases</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually...I think a vital strategy. It's important to remember if an opponent can't contribute to combat, then crashing them knocks them out. But I've found this a good way to include high soak enemies with moderate hardness and not have them feel like invincible brick walls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338627#post1338627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-area attacks / ganging up on 1 person being extremely powerful by the nature of the system, meaning a full circle can defeat nearly any non-legendary size threat just by sheer initiative advantage and aoe enemies become exponentially stronger the more enemies they fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, others have said &quot;But Solars should be that good!&quot; and I think that's true but also missing the point. The Devs have a qoute, which some variation of exists around the world: Even Hercules couldn't stand against two. Exalted's source material rarely treats fighting multiple meaningful opponents as an easy task--and frankly, you need stuff like that for some of the settings ideas to make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:39:17-07:00","id":1338671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338669#post1338669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly a post in Ask the devs stated that Might is supposed to emule Charms, so that battlegroup do not use them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While that is correct, nothing in the book really states it, and frankly Might bonuses are not in and of themselves good enough to represent Charms, much less when crazy stuff like Principle of Motion are among those Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:40:19-07:00","id":1338672,"title":"","content":"Also the point about your circle being too strong for every solo ennemy is totally fair. <br /> <br /> However, i think many people encounter the following hardship (I did and other friends at least) : <br /> <br /> Its hard to put multiple ennemies at almost maximum fighting level capacities in order to contest your PC because you feel like &quot;is it right that I'm using multiple litteral world champion of dexterity and melee almost everywhere ?&quot; Because you feel like it's supposed to be rare. And it is actually rare, it's just more interesting if they are in the PC's way<br /> <br /> As a ST i spend much time on the PC by helping the players design, customize, etc them. But when I design the NPCs I usually have way less time to do this, resulting in them being less powerful<br /> <br /> I really feel like it gets better with time, but you really need practice as a ST to adjust everything. It's not like DD4 where even if you are a newcomer, there are thousands of tables to follow if you want to balance en encounter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T12:51:41-07:00","id":1338675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338643#post1338643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know of any alternate systems but some of your problems might have some built in mitigation that you\u2019re not taking full advantage of?<br /> <br /> I have to admit I don\u2019t really get this one. I think that a full circle of Solars really SHOULD kick all kinds of ass against one single enemy. That\u2019s balanced by the fact that most great enemies have the resources of several nations at their disposal. If your PCs reach Alhat to fight him with even half their resources unspent you may have terribly underestimated the power that a directional war god commands.<br /> <br /> Also AoE attacks are you referring to? Are we talking like Death of Obsidian Butterfies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that ganging up turns any combatants into super soldiers, not just a Circle of Solars. For instance, a Solar who can defeat Octavian can still lose to 5-6 mortal soldiers so long as they are individual combatants rather than a size 1 battlegroup.<br /> <br /> For AoE, I'm thinking of area attacks that grant significant initiative from each target hit. I was sorta traumatized by a certain wolf emanation in Tomb of Dreams, who became ultra-deadly because we had 7 combatants and his Combat Charm makes a Withering against all targets. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338643#post1338643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain these further? Do you mean like not hitting allies to farm initiative off them?</div> </div> </div> </div> The rule you mention is fairly clear cut to me, I'm thinking more of rules like how the ST has to adjudicate when Withering Attacks no longer award initiative, or decide when Withering 1 enemy and Decisive-ing another is considered cheating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338643#post1338643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think strictly speaking this is true. Twenty bloodapes are absolutely more deadly run as individuals than in a battlegroup, but I think they\u2019re more deadly than a single one for sure.<br /> <br /> A BG of 20 apes though is like one ape that can attack everything in short range, has 21 health levels healable with rally for numbers, 6 parry, 9 soak, an attack with 15 accuracy and 19 damage, can boost that with command rolls, and who doesn\u2019t give up more than 1 initiative to withering attacks unless they deplete a magnitude in which case they get 6.<br /> <br /> Also RAW if you have 4 initiative and a battlegroup deals 10 damage to you, the first 4 crash you and the next 6 deal decisive damage in the one attack.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not going to kill a whole circle on their own like 20 individual apes might, but paired with a commander like Sigereth or Octavian or an Exalted commander and they can do some serious damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure a commander <i>can</i> make a blood ape battle group deadlier than an individual blood-ape, but without a commander 1 Exalt vs 20 blood apes is comparable in difficulty to 1 Exalt vs 1 blood ape given the lone blood ape gets to use their Charms. The battle group actually becomes strictly weaker if using the RAW rules that battle groups cannot damage you with the same attack that crashed you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-30-2019, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T13:15:06-07:00","id":1338681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338659#post1338659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sincerely hope you find what you're looking for. (Following the thread with interest.) But almost every subsystem over every single edition of Exalted relies on the ST and players putting effort into not breaking the system.<br /> <br /> I've never seen a robust set of houserules that addresses this -- but you're probably looking for complete rewrites like Exalted : Reincarnated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to figure out how much can be improved without rebuilding everything from the ground up. If it turns out the system must be heavily modded to be fixed I'll probably just settle for minor changes rather than throw everything out the window.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338659#post1338659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think you should run Mutants and Masterminds. The system isn't impossible to break, but it's pretty difficult -- especially if you insist on every Power being modelled on a published Exalted Charm. M&amp;M solves all your issues apart from &quot;conservation of ninjutsu&quot; (which is <i>massively</i> exacerbated).</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I'll check it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338659#post1338659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The only way of fixing this is to track Initative on every combatant for every combatant... which is massively math intensive. Momentum doesn't try to address it (and Reincarnated is a system rewrite to the scale of Dungeons the Dragonning). I guess the advice on page 194 of the Corebook <i>kinda</i> helps? (SHENANIGANS!) But you don't need homebrew to apply that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having initiative subtracks for each combatant pairing is the sort of added complication I'd rather avoid (yeah I know, I want to have my cake and eat it too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). One thing I'm thinking of trying out is pooling initiative so that all combatants on the same side add/substract from the same pool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338659#post1338659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2a. Area attacks typically only award Initative from one target. Where they don't, houserule they do to fix that. Simples.</div> </div> </div> </div>good advice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338659#post1338659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2b. I'd be tempted to do something like FFG Edge of the Empire and give Boss characters two Initative tracks (a bit like how Single Point Form works). But this is kinda a feature of the system -- the Exalted (especially Solars) are the biggest bads in the setting. Each individual PC is a world shaping powerhouse, that Wyld Hunts want to gang up on at least 5-to-1. If the Circle gets a numerical advantage... well they're <i>supposed</i> to wipe the floor with their foes. No &quot;but what about&quot; -- the Exalted wrested Creation from the <i>nigh omnipotent beings from beyond reality who birthed dieties to serve them as slaves</i>. They're supposed to be able to kick the ass of <i>anything</i> in the setting, and to kick the ass of <i>most things</i> even when outnumberered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done that before with a Behemoth, giving them 2 initiative tracks to emulate their power level without having to come up with a whole Charmset. It worked well, but it would be weird on a &quot;normal&quot; foe to suddenly have multiple initiative tracks.<br /> <br /> On a similar vein, the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/272809/The-Thousand-Sanctioned-Beasts--Martial-Artists\" target=\"_blank\">Thousand Sanctioned Beasts : Martial Artists</a> on Storyteller's Vault has an &quot;Ultimate Foe&quot; which is a Celestial Martial Artist who gets to attack as many times as he has enemies +1. Again this succeeds at creating the level of challenge needed for a Circle of Exalts to struggle against a single enemy, but the decision to grant them tons of free attacks feels sorta arbitrary to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338659#post1338659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. &quot;plz don't do dis&quot; is basically the Storyteller's Guide for Exalted. It's practically the slogan of the gameline. You need to houserule and you need players who'll work with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, thanks for the reminder. Ultimately I don't think the system can be reduced purely to maths, but I'm still hoping I can make it a bit more consistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338659#post1338659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. If battlegroups are posing that much of an issue, then don't use them. Roll in 20 individual Blood Apes. Or once the battgroup is defeated, roll in a single survivor as an individual combatant. Or cheat the battlegroup's stats higher. Or don't use the combat system and run the encounter narratively. Use the advice on page 212.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately the innate advantage from greater numbers means that 20 individual blood apes will be just as overpowered as a single battlegroup of blood apes is underpowered. I routinely make dramatic encounters that don't use the battle engine but usually it's for encounters that aren't important to the Story - an army is rarely a random encounter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-30-2019, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T14:09:49-07:00","id":1338688,"title":"","content":"One way to make battlegroups more tough could be to give them something similar to Legendary Size, bypassed by area of effect attacks. This way a single slash from a daiklave can't cut all the enemies, force the character to specialize (purchasing aoe charms) and make the bgs last longer in the fight.<br /> <br /> For the problem with multiple combatant, give the boss counterattack/aoe/multiattack powers, some encounter to consume resources before the fight and battlegroups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12370,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12370-lddm84","user":"LDDM84","date":". 09-30-2019, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12370-lddm84","name":"LDDM84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T14:29:09-07:00","id":1338694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LDDM84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338688#post1338688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This way a single slash from a daiklave can't cut all the enemies\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cA single slash from a daiklave\u201d <b>already</b> doesn\u2019t \u201ccut all the enemies\u201d in a battle group - Magnitude damage doesn\u2019t <i>just</i> represent the physical health of the assembled troops, but <i>also</i> their morale and other abstract factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338675#post1338675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that ganging up turns any combatants into super soldiers, not just a Circle of Solars. For instance, a Solar who can defeat Octavian can still lose to 5-6 mortal soldiers so long as they are individual combatants rather than a size 1 battlegroup.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might not like the rule, but it\u2019s not a bug - the system is working as intended. If those five mortal soldiers are important enough to the story to be represented individually, then the Solar <i>should</i> have a rough time with them, even if he\u2019s capable of wrestling demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-30-2019, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T15:26:14-07:00","id":1338699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338675#post1338675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant that ganging up turns any combatants into super soldiers, not just a Circle of Solars. For instance, a Solar who can defeat Octavian can still lose to 5-6 mortal soldiers so long as they are individual combatants rather than a size 1 battlegroup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but that's the system working as intended.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338670#post1338670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devs have a qoute, which some variation of exists around the world: Even Hercules couldn't stand against two. Exalted's source material rarely treats fighting multiple meaningful opponents as an easy task</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the system working as intended. OP was complaining about when the PCs outnumber their enemies, not vice versa.<br /> <br /> I do think battlegroups could do with a buff. 100 troops should be ten times deadlier than 10 troops. But ganging up and the action economy is working as intended.<br /> <br /> Et tu Brute/For the Watch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T15:53:54-07:00","id":1338705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338699#post1338699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but that's the system working as intended.<br /> <br /> Also the system working as intended. OP was complaining about when the PCs outnumber their enemies, not vice versa.<br /> <br /> I do think battlegroups could do with a buff. 100 troops should be ten times deadlier than 10 troops. But ganging up and the action economy is working as intended.<br /> <br /> Et tu Brute/For the Watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just specifying why \u201csolars should be that good\u201d wasn\u2019t the end all of the matter. BGs...I think are actually really good, but a layer of that is how often they get a stratagem off. Lord knows an Ambushing Battlegroup is terrifying.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also Engage. engage can really really hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 09-30-2019, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T17:13:46-07:00","id":1338711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338675#post1338675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that ganging up turns any combatants into super soldiers, not just a Circle of Solars. For instance, a Solar who can defeat Octavian can still lose to 5-6 mortal soldiers so long as they are individual combatants rather than a size 1 battlegroup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, and I'm not one to try and promote Solars going balls crazy optimized, but Bulwark Stance and Fivefold Bulwark Stance, especially with Hail Shattering Practice, can make that kind of thing 100% possible. Absent those charms, or Circle of Bright Reaving or other ones like them, it is hard, but supposedly 5-6 mortals who aren't grouped into a battlegroup are 5-6 of some of the greatest mortal heroes ever.<br /> <br /> So it's not just 5-6 random guys, they'd be turned into a size 1 battlegroup. It's like Azal Aresh, legendary demonhunter with arrowheads made from the teeth of slain blood apes, Serafina Prinus grandmaster of five animal styles of martial arts, Xian Miu of the Green Blade who weaves a deadly tapestry through the battlefield with his poisoned blade, Vareesh Liang deadly master of kunai who can peg the chink in a suit of fullplate from twenty yards, One River who's strength is so great they can lift and throw a fully grown warhorse, and Pupup the nimble forest hermit who shocked the entire city by being able to loose her third arrow into the bullseye before the first one struck home.<br /> <br /> If your Solar is facing all of them, alone, without Bulwark Stance that's going to be a rough time, but I do feel like it should be. Not every mortal needs to matter individually when compared to the mightiest of exalted, there <i>needs </i>to be room in the game to tear though a room full of mooks, but at a certain point great enough heroes should be able to put up a fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338675#post1338675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For AoE, I'm thinking of area attacks that grant significant initiative from each target hit. I was sorta traumatized by a certain wolf emanation in Tomb of Dreams, who became ultra-deadly because we had 7 combatants and his Combat Charm makes a Withering against all targets. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, that's a pretty special exception. I'm actually not quite sure why it's worded the way it is, because I think every other withering AoE in the game at best takes the highest initiative from the attack and gains one additional initiative for each target hit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338675#post1338675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule you mention is fairly clear cut to me, I'm thinking more of rules like how the ST has to adjudicate when Withering Attacks no longer award initiative, or decide when Withering 1 enemy and Decisive-ing another is considered cheating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for the former it's a bit hard but mostly a kind of &quot;Oh crap.&quot; strategy for when you accidentally put a character into combat who really shouldn't have been there, and is clearly just going to be giving the PCs initiative way way too easily. Like you accidentally added in a single zombie into the combat or something, who should only ever be a battlegroup or a trivial opponent. Or possibly when an opponent is in their -4s with a ton of effects stacked on them to make them impossible to miss.<br /> <br /> For the later case I'd be pretty lenient, although with the caveat that designing encounters for Solars is really hard and you sometimes need to get creative with how badass the enemies are and their tactics. As long as there's not a mega wide divide between combatants, like there's a tough guy and a few less tough ones and maybe a battlegroup it's okay, just as long as there's not two deadly Dusk caste Abyssals and one single mortal in rags that you can just annihilate for 60 initiative before turning it on the Exalted foes.<br /> <br /> If it's just the two legendary Dusk castes though, and maybe a huge battlegroup of zombies, then crashing one Abyssal to launch a decisive at the other is dangerous enough that it's worth the risk.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338675#post1338675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sure a commander <i>can</i> make a blood ape battle group deadlier than an individual blood-ape, but without a commander 1 Exalt vs 20 blood apes is comparable in difficulty to 1 Exalt vs 1 blood ape given the lone blood ape gets to use their Charms. The battle group actually becomes strictly weaker if using the RAW rules that battle groups cannot damage you with the same attack that crashed you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not STRICTLY weaker exactly. The battlegroup doesn't lose stats and gain nothing, although I'd argue that it's at least close. A regular ape has 9 health levels and starts getting dice penalties as they're taken away, also they can be crashed and give their enemy a huge initiative bonus, a battlegroup has 21 health levels and is pretty much 100% combat effective right down to the last one.<br /> <br /> Either way, I've been looking around trying to find the dev quote that says Might is there to represent charms, and can't, what I DID find was a ton of player and Storyteller advice saying to just let them have charms, or that it was obvious they're supposed to have charms. For one, hilariously, a battlegroup of Blood Apes that can't use charms can't materialize, so unless they're already material when the fight starts they're completely useless. I think this might be an orichalcum rule thing if nothing else. If you feel like Might does not properly represent charms for battlegroups of supernatural enemies, which I agree it doesn't, then allow them to use their charms too, which I recommend anyway.<br /> <br /> Which to me makes a whole hell of a lot of sense. A battlegroup that has bonuses from Size, Might, and Drill and using Principle of Motion still isn't remotely as strong as a legit straight 20 heroic Blood Apes in combat, so why not? The only time I'd urge caution on this is maybe, maybe, for a group of 5 Dragonblooded or something. If you let a bunch of Elite Drill, Might 3 DBs use Dragonblooded charms that might get out of hand. Then again the book expressly says Dragonblooded are almost never battlegrouped, so that shouldn't be a huge issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T17:17:42-07:00","id":1338713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338711#post1338711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5-6 mortals who aren't grouped into a battlegroup are 5-6 of some of the greatest mortal heroes ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or at least important to the story. They don't have to be statted like combat gods; it just needs to be clear that these people aren't minions to be mowed down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T17:33:30-07:00","id":1338716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338713#post1338713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or at least important to the story. They don't have to be statted like combat gods; it just needs to be clear that these people aren't minions to be mowed down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that\u2019s true, although at 6 to 1 odds without group fighting charms they don\u2019t really need to be. Unless they\u2019re all stooped little bureaucrats or something, which swings back to probably not going very far anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T17:40:10-07:00","id":1338718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338713#post1338713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or at least important to the story. They don't have to be statted like combat gods; it just needs to be clear that these people aren't minions to be mowed down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Characters who are important to the story (so not BGs) but are not opponents who can meaningfully combat the PCs are trivial opponents, even if individual ones, so being a BG would actually be better than being important but unable to oppose the PCs, when it comes to fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T18:59:55-07:00","id":1338729,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm not saying don't change the system if it's not working for you, just that the system might handle better if you took different tactics with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T19:28:39-07:00","id":1338733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338729#post1338729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm not saying don't change the system if it's not working for you, just that the system might handle better if you took different tactics with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, everyone is making good points.<br /> <br /> About the 5-6 combatants trumping the one Exalt, I see the point you and others are making that they should basically be a battle group or trivial opponents if they're not significant threats. I guess I just need to get used to the notion that the Combat Engine works from the assumption that every combatant is meaningful until the ST makes them a trivial opponent by fiat.<br /> <br /> On battle groups, letting battle groups use Charms is an interesting idea, I'll probably try it out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T21:38:19-07:00","id":1338743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338733#post1338733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries, everyone is making good points.<br /> <br /> About the 5-6 combatants trumping the one Exalt, I see the point you and others are making that they should basically be a battle group or trivial opponents if they're not significant threats. I guess I just need to get used to the notion that the Combat Engine works from the assumption that every combatant is meaningful until the ST makes them a trivial opponent by fiat.<br /> <br /> On battle groups, letting battle groups use Charms is an interesting idea, I'll probably try it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, although that level can change depending on the exact setting and combatant numbers. There's a level where foes are so weak that they're not rolled in no matter how many there are. An entire 500 man counting-house of scribes and clerks just isn't going to be rolled into combat between your Dawn and the Essence 5 Ragara Master of Coin. They might even be so thick in the room as to count as difficult terrain, and they're STILL not getting an initiative track.<br /> <br /> Then past that there's guys like joe realm soldier or guard. Those guys are not being rolled into combat as single people, or even in <a href=\"https://www.worldanvil.com/uploads/images/e2713352473a1a0a1d51d81322bbb2f8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">groups of 2-3</a>. If a fight breaks out and one side has a pair of shlubs in helmets as guards, they're not getting rolled in, they're just scenery. In universe they technically have a chance of contributing, but it's so small and their narrative presence is so light that they're not counted. They only get rolled in if you've got <a href=\"https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/001/159/287/large/dmitry-burmak-fg-soldiers.jpg?1441272207\" target=\"_blank\">8-10 of them</a>, at that point there's just too many trained swords, they cross the threshold from being scenery to being at least somewhat dangerous. If they're elite guards against one single foe, you might roll in 2 of them as individuals beside the DB, but they'd have to be strong enough that their presence is a threat, not a boon to the Solar.<br /> <br /> Also typically battlegroups represent relatively homogeneous groups working together. They're forming a battle line, or surrounding a fugitive together, that kind of thing. Then you have a <a href=\"https://images-wixmp-ed30a86b8c4ca887773594c2.wixmp.com/f/6fcd12ac-7339-4669-a859-55322ed71f8a/d57515a-3ad92659-367e-44b5-82c4-4e5e9385172e.jpg?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..EvJslg3827zGeu9Kr_nBy6nTB7fhFSmZ9vb4VzrcIFs\" target=\"_blank\">class of hero</a> that you would not field in a battlegroup. They're just too <a href=\"https://nwfilm.org/app/uploads/2016/11/SevenSamurai_1954.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">unique and strong</a>. They're the kind's of mortal hero that may include bringing down an Exalt in their legend someday. If they don't meet that criteria, they're either a battlegroups or background.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you're having some trouble with that from the ST side, don't be afraid to get a little epic with the antagonists in the game either. The Scarlet Empress's 'mortal' bodyguards are giant elite warriors with disturbingly fast and effective sign language, iron will, superhuman strength, and extra powers granted to them by alchemy and sorcery. So you'd think with that awesomeness she'd have like 100, maybe 150? Nope, 5,000 of them.<br /> <br /> With your PCs, if they're going after a really big important antagonist, there should be at least one fight battled to conclusion before they even see the foe, maybe as many as two or three, and then when they reach them it should be the big bad, maybe one or two really impressive allies, and then a big elite battlegroup of some kind. There aren't many foes in the world of Exalted that you can't justify that for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T00:01:21-07:00","id":1338752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338718#post1338718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters who are important to the story (so not BGs) but are not opponents who can meaningfully combat the PCs are trivial opponents, even if individual ones...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but whether an opponent is able to meaningfully combat the PCs <i>is an ST call</i>. It's not tied to how many dots in Melee you have.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Especially considering how folks keep mentioning the Dawn, as opposed to the Eclipse who hasn't raised his Dexterity or given Combat Abilities above 3. Those baseline soldiers in the Core book have a pretty good chance of seriously wounding him depending on a bunch of factors.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-01-2019, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:37:56-07:00","id":1338792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338752#post1338752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Especially considering how folks keep mentioning the Dawn, as opposed to the Eclipse who hasn't raised his Dexterity or given Combat Abilities above 3. Those baseline soldiers in the Core book have a pretty good chance of seriously wounding him depending on a bunch of factors.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m legitimately curious how often you encounter this yourself. From what I\u2019ve seen at a few different tables the temptation to just toss a pair of bonus points and a specialty at melee or brawl or something just ends up being too great. It\u2019s such a small percentage of your chargen resources, and you end up rocking a parry of 6, an attack pool of 11, and a big excellency cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:43:35-07:00","id":1338793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338792#post1338792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m legitimately curious how often you encounter this yourself. From what I\u2019ve seen at a few different tables the temptation to just toss a pair of bonus points and a specialty at melee or brawl or something just ends up being too great. It\u2019s such a small percentage of your chargen resources, and you end up rocking a parry of 6, an attack pool of 11, and a big excellency cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah quite the same. The only few time someone didn't go full score in fighting ability it was really core to the concept or he changed it few sessions later with experience","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:48:25-07:00","id":1338795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338792#post1338792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m legitimately curious how often you encounter this yourself. From what I\u2019ve seen at a few different tables the temptation to just toss a pair of bonus points and a specialty at melee or brawl or something just ends up being too great. It\u2019s such a small percentage of your chargen resources, and you end up rocking a parry of 6, an attack pool of 11, and a big excellency cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's common for Twilights and Eclipses at my tables, for instance my E3 Twilight went against Ahlat with 3 awareness / 3 Melee and no Excellency in either one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T07:58:42-07:00","id":1338797,"title":"","content":"Knight Raiton started with Brawl 3 and Dexterity 4 (I think, but this was more than a year ago; honestly, it might've just been a 3), with his only Brawl Charm being Fists of Iron Technique. In the time it took to reach Essence 3, he's raised Brawl to 5 and picked up the Charms necessary to reach Knockout Blow. His Dexterity is still 4.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpider started out with Dexterity 5, but still hasn't raised his Melee above 3 (though he did take a specialty in defense).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-01-2019, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T09:53:25-07:00","id":1338820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338793#post1338793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah quite the same. The only few time someone didn't go full score in fighting ability it was really core to the concept or he changed it few sessions later with experience</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my last two characters were a Dawn that I wanted to play through finding and becoming a martial arts master, and a Twilight master sorcerer who was particularly in desperate need of allies for protection, so I made them both intentionally pretty sub-par to start. <br /> <br /> Other than that, out of the 20 characters in the past 4 games I can remember 14 of them had max combat abilities off chargen and those are just the ones I\u2019m sure of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T10:07:15-07:00","id":1338825,"title":"","content":"Different people play differently; having the decision on what makes an opponent trivial be an ST call seems even more appropriate with this revelation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T10:28:07-07:00","id":1338828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338820#post1338820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, my last two characters were a Dawn that I wanted to play through finding and becoming a martial arts master, and a Twilight master sorcerer who was particularly in desperate need of allies for protection, so I made them both intentionally pretty sub-par to start.<br /> <br /> Other than that, out of the 20 characters in the past 4 games I can remember 14 of them had max combat abilities off chargen and those are just the ones I\u2019m sure of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I realized recently (watched the first episodes of Demon Slayer) that I really like the trope of training and stuff but it's pretty hard to do in Exalted because the characters for which it is usually important (fighters, etc ...) starts out by being the absolute best in the world, so it doesn't really leave any place for &quot;improvement&quot;. I guess training for Charms could fulfill that function but I haven't been able to pull that off in an interesting manner yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T12:31:30-07:00","id":1338855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338828#post1338828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I realized recently (watched the first episodes of Demon Slayer) that I really like the trope of training and stuff but it's pretty hard to do in Exalted because the characters for which it is usually important (fighters, etc ...) starts out by being the absolute best in the world, so it doesn't really leave any place for &amp;quot;improvement&amp;quot;. I guess training for Charms could fulfill that function but I haven't been able to pull that off in an interesting manner yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what\u2019s more three of best combat scenes I\u2019ve ever been part of in 3e were right at the start of the campaign when I had 3 dex and 1 brawl. The first one was the first combat with that character ever, in a kind of gastro-teahouse. A bar brawl broke out, I got crashed into the furniture, came back swinging, narrowly dodged the next attack, locked in a clinch, and then hurled the guy straight out the front door and skidding across the dirt road.<br /> <br /> Then the next one was a street fight, it started out okay, trading blows with my personal essence letting me keep up, until their friend in heavy armor busted onto the scene anyway. I think could have beaten them but not without showing my castemark, so I had to get clever and pick up an entire cart, upending it on the elite guy like a cage and then booking it. <br /> <br /> I distinctly remember the next two fights, one against a horde of beastmen when the bear leader and I had it out Greco-Roman wrestle style, and the one after that where we actually used unhorse gambits and athletics charms to try and keep up with the outrider vanguard of an invading army, but after that it starts to get a bit hazy. I only really remember the final fight after that and I have a sneaky suspicion it\u2019s because that was six or seven sessions in and I\u2019d been funnelling all my xp and Solar do into martial arts and everything was just getting one-two smackdowned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T13:19:16-07:00","id":1338859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338733#post1338733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries, everyone is making good points.<br /> <br /> About the 5-6 combatants trumping the one Exalt, I see the point you and others are making that they should basically be a battle group or trivial opponents if they're not significant threats. I guess I just need to get used to the notion that the Combat Engine works from the assumption that every combatant is meaningful until the ST makes them a trivial opponent by fiat.<br /> <br /> On battle groups, letting battle groups use Charms is an interesting idea, I'll probably try it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers thing is a pretty constant factor across all RPGs-- it's REALLY hard to balance a single boss against a group. If you inflate their defense too much it becomes frustrating; if you boost their offense too much you wind up getting, like, one turn where you annhiliate a single PC, then you get beaten down in short order. (And that only gets worse in a system like Exalted where one character can be orders of magnitude better at fighting than another). The problem isn't numbers, it's action economy, and you can't really solve that without giving bosses more actions than any individual player can muster.<br /> <br /> Mutants and Masterminds was mentioned earlier. I've actually used it to run Exalted, and it works... fairly well*, though you lose a lot of the non-combat depth that makes Exalted so fun. But even then, with a group that's pretty heterogeneous in terms of combat power, I have to give bosses extra turns if the party gets much over 3 characters. <br /> <br /> If you don't want to go down that route, the best you can do is to pack a lot of cheap reflexive abilities. Miss me in melee? I counterattack and throw you down the street! Start pulling a bow? I get to toss a knife at the string! Flank me? I dodge and leave the two of you swinging at each other! <br /> <br /> *As long as everyone goes gonzo on their powers-- M&amp;M is pretty bad at distinguishing, say, two martial artists. Unless one of them is using kung-fu magic to have his sword fly around the room and the other is transforming into a bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 10-01-2019, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T13:44:19-07:00","id":1338863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338859#post1338859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*As long as everyone goes gonzo on their powers-- M&amp;M is pretty bad at distinguishing, say, two martial artists. Unless one of them is using kung-fu magic to have his sword fly around the room and the other is transforming into a bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. That's what stunting is for.<br /> <br /> And I'd make the PCs base their powers on the published Charms, including prereqs, mapped as faithfully as possible (which won't be very faithfully in M&amp;M -- but PL is so easy to balance and design encounters around, it doesn't really matter if the PCs do go gonzo).<br /> <br /> To simplfy M&amp;M somewhat:<br /> It's a system designed for players to invent their own super heroes and hand craft their powers from scratch.<br /> All characters have a Power Level which determines the strength of their attacks and defences.<br /> Robin is PL 8, Nightwing is PL 10, Batman is PL 12 and Superman is (the extreme upper boarder of) PL 15.<br /> When Robin punches someone, it's a PL 8 attack. Batman's punches are PL 12. Batman's Batrangs are also PL 12. The machine guns on the Batmobile are ALSO PL 12. Whether Superman is punching you, using his ice breath or his heat vision, all his attacks are PL 15.<br /> This makes designing encounters a breeze.<br /> <br /> In play, you don't say &quot;Batman punches you for PL 12, then Aquaman also punches you for PL 12, then the Flash punches you for PL 12&quot;. That's like saying &quot;I Wither him to gain some Initative&quot;.<br /> <br /> The way you differentiate Snake Style from Tiger Style is Stunting -- because in M&amp;M you'll be making PL 14 Unarmed attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-01-2019, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T20:47:54-07:00","id":1338922,"title":"","content":"Going back to the original post.<br /> <br /> This is the hack known as Glory Overwhelming made by Lumi in the Exalted Discord. It gives you infinite motes. Some charms break, but believe or not turned out fairly well in play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fMnvGMIEMnPS3qZqEQRLnTZw0G--K899GAKyIwmDNyk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fMnvGMIEMnPS3qZqEQRLnTZw0G--K899GAKyIwmDNyk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fMnvGMIEMnPS3qZqEQRLnTZw0G--K899GAKyIwmDNyk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fMnvGMIEMnPS3qZqEQRLnTZw0G--K899GAKyIwmDNyk/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's also another one called Hissatsu which gives infinite initiative for attacks, but I haven't played that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T22:28:33-07:00","id":1338943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338922#post1338922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to the original post.<br /> <br /> This is the hack known as Glory Overwhelming made by Lumi in the Exalted Discord. It gives you infinite motes. Some charms break, but believe or not turned out fairly well in play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fMnvGMIEMnPS3qZqEQRLnTZw0G--K899GAKyIwmDNyk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fMnvGMIEMnPS3qZqEQRLnTZw0G--K899GAKyIwmDNyk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fMnvGMIEMnPS3qZqEQRLnTZw0G--K899GAKyIwmDNyk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fMnvGMIEMnPS3qZqEQRLnTZw0G--K899GAKyIwmDNyk/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's also another one called Hissatsu which gives infinite initiative for attacks, but I haven't played that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh Glory Overwhelming looks like a lot of fun. And I very much like what Hissatsu is trying to do.<br /> <br /> Is there an actual document for Hissatsu? I can only find blurbs and excerpts on the Discord.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T14:51:03-07:00","id":1339068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338863#post1338863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. That's what stunting is for.<br /> <br /> And I'd make the PCs base their powers on the published Charms, including prereqs, mapped as faithfully as possible (which won't be very faithfully in M&amp;M -- but PL is so easy to balance and design encounters around, it doesn't really matter if the PCs do go gonzo).</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, Stunting gets old if there's not enough crunch (relative to the rest of the system, at least) to back it up. M&amp;M can do... fairly well, but obviously not as well as an absurdly crunchy game like Exalted.<br /> <br /> For reference, the &quot;Exalts and Excellencies&quot; character I played in that campaign had these &quot;charms&quot; <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Eye of a Thousand Battles</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Perception Affliction 5 (Vulnerable and Impaired, resisted and overcome by Fighting), double limited degree, limited: only against you, Subtle, Insideous</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Iron Whirlwind</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Multiattack on Damage 8; Variable Descriptor 1: Any weapon/unarmed, Subtle</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Celestial Fencing Technique</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Feature 3: No attack roll on close attack, Penetrating 7, Incurable; Variable Descriptor 1: Any weapon/unarmed</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Body-Annihilating Strike</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Close Affliction 8 (impaired, disabled, incapacitated, resisted and overcome by Fortitude), Subtle</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Flawless General Technique</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">luck control 2 (spend points on allies, force rerolls); 4 luck; subtle; sense-dependant (hearing)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Sevenfold Step</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Teleport 3 (accurate, limited: must move through intervening space)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Marathon Step Technique</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Speed 2, Activation (move)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Ox Body Technique</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Healing 1 (Reaction, Effortless, Limited to Self, Limited to degree of damage dealt by the last attack)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Ancient Warlord's Knowledge</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Danger Sense; Precognition, Limited to Martial matters, DC 13 Exp: War check required</td> </tr> </table></div> So, like, some good stuff, some unique stuff, but another melee fighter is probably going to have a lot of similar powers. It gets worse the farther you go from combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To simplfy M&amp;M somewhat... </div> </div> </div>Eh... sort of?<br /> <br /> M&amp;M is a d20 game with a build-your-own-superpowers structure. There are discreet list of Effects and Modifiers, which you combine to make unique abilities. A lightsaber, a mind-melting psychic attack, and a missile might all be built off the Damage effect, but with different Modifiers to make them behave differently. It is not built around attrition in the <i>slightest, </i>nor does it stop to think about what it means that I can, say, get myself the ability to turn dirt into gold for 2 power points (out of 150 points for a standard starting character). There's a certain amount of player buy-in required to keep from obliterating the setting or breaking the custom power system wide open, but the latter is tempered by the fact that it's usually really obvious (to everyone) when you're doing something Wrong.<br /> <br /> It achieves balance through Power Levels, which impose hard caps on all of your numbers. On skills, the limit is high enough that it's not worth worrying about; for combat stuff, the neat thing is that the limits are in the form of <i>sums</i>. Your attack roll plus your damage can't exceed <i>this.</i> If you want to be hard to hurt, you're forced to be easy to hit. Stuff like that. That's how you can get Batman and Superman in the same party (or at least Robin and Superboy)-- Batman makes up for power with accuracy and evasiveness. (In theory, at least-- in practice, if you trade off too far in any direction you run into math problems, so it's best for Batman to pack some C4 and high-PL nerve strikes just in case). If you've seen shows like Justice League Unlimited or Young Justice, it winds up being exactly that sort of paradigm, where Wonder Woman flies around punching tanks while Green Arrow shoots explosive arrows that are equally effective, and then they both get blasted across the room by the same burst of lightning.<br /> <br /> Putting together powers takes some getting used to, and the damage system is a little odd-- the victim rolls a save instead of the attacker rolling damage-- but it plays fast, smooth, and is gloriously fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 10-02-2019, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T02:19:18-07:00","id":1339146,"title":"","content":"Yeah, M&amp;M is pretty fast and fun. This Tuesday we had a Boku no Hero-inspired game, my first M&amp;M game, and I liked it a lot.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u00b4t use it for Exalted because I like Exalted\u00b4s system, but that game is fast and fun.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:00:42-07:00","id":1339180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1339146#post1339146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn\u00b4t use it for Exalted because I like Exalted\u00b4s system, but that game is fast and fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I prefer Wild Talents -- another build your own super hero game. It's a LOT wonkier than M&amp;M, and needs real buy in from the players and ST in terms of powers (one of the default powers is &quot;Invincibility&quot; which is exactly what it says on the tin, but &quot;Suppress Nuclear Fusion&quot; to turn off the sun &quot;Teleport... hostile target to the black hole in the center of the galaxy&quot; and &quot;Knock Out All Villains And Ne'er-do-wells In A 500 Foot Radius&quot; all deserve an honourable mention and &quot;Infinite Life Span&quot; is considered a &quot;dud&quot; power). But the mechanical system is the One Roll Engine -- because it resolves basically any given action in a single roll. Very fast paced.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewizardsworkshop.proboards.com/thread/433/dtd-books\" target=\"_blank\">Dungeons The Dragonning</a> is a parody game based on numerous RPGs including Exalted. Fidelity to Exalted is pretty low, things don't map precisely and there's a lot of zaney elements that need curtailing, but it's pretty well balanced and it's free. It's on the extreme end of fan rewrites though. Still a suprising number of Exaltations work for Solars (I think they default map to Atlantean, but Paragon or Chosen should work just fine), and there's a Dragon-Blooded Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Glory Overwhelming looks very interesting though. It'd be keen to try that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:15:14-07:00","id":1339183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1339180#post1339180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glory Overwhelming looks very interesting though. It'd be keen to try that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I actually kind of think that it's take on essence works better for the fiction than the default-- right now there's &quot;don't spend too much or you'll be hit by roleplaying consequences&quot; in the form of the anima, which makes sense, and &quot;don't spend too much because you have a limited supply,&quot; which doesn't feel quite so fitting for heroic demigods. I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T09:13:30-07:00","id":1339198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1339183#post1339183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I actually kind of think that it's take on essence works better for the fiction than the default-- right now there's &quot;don't spend too much or you'll be hit by roleplaying consequences&quot; in the form of the anima, which makes sense, and &quot;don't spend too much because you have a limited supply,&quot; which doesn't feel quite so fitting for heroic demigods. I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One thing I really like from the new Aberrant is that you can take on Flux (think of it as Limit that gives you Derangements and or mutations) to restore their version of motes, and that if you totally run out, and don't want to take flux, you can take what amounts to health levels to keep digging.<br /> <br /> It would take some finagling to port over to Exalted, to the point that Glory Overwhelming might just be easier at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T09:03:45-07:00","id":1339385,"title":"","content":"I'd consider something like &quot;every X motes you spend increases your anima by 1; if you're already at bondfire, instead gain a point of limit. Reset at sunset.&quot; That keeps some incentive to not overspend and some consequence for going whole-hog without adding any new mechanics to an already-complicated game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 10-04-2019, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T09:33:31-07:00","id":1339392,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm wondering is how Scion 2E's Storypath system would translate to Exalted. The rework of the 9 Attributes into approaches to a problem looks like a smart improvement at first glance. Plus It has a system of Scale to model power differences between 2 opponents, which gives more ways to categorize enemies than &quot;trivial&quot; and &quot;non-trivial&quot;.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have experience with Scion 2E and how it compares to Ex3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T04:44:23-07:00","id":1339569,"title":"","content":"The main thing I'm starting to consider for house rules is some tweaks to battle groups.<br /> <br /> The area attack is potentially a bit of a problem. There's often not much variation in defence values so the attack tends to either flounder ineffectually like what a lot of people seem to experience or roll really well and be capable of putting the entire circle on the backfoot (barring the use of charms that can be activated after the roll has already taken place).<br /> <br /> I think my preference would be to borrow from the rules for Environmental Hazards because in practice I've found that if the players are rolling vs. a fixed difficulty it's more likely that a couple of them will fail despite having good dice pools on paper. There's some disadvantages to the fix, most notably the more I smooth out the irregularities the harder it becomes harder to translate the individual profile into a battle group profile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T15:15:26-07:00","id":1339932,"title":"","content":"I'm personally toying with the idea of making battle groups into active initiative wielding guys. The main issue is revamping of the math (mainly bonuses size and command rolls provide)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T04:23:18-07:00","id":1340012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1339569#post1339569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing I'm starting to consider for house rules is some tweaks to battle groups.<br /> <br /> The area attack is potentially a bit of a problem. There's often not much variation in defence values so the attack tends to either flounder ineffectually like what a lot of people seem to experience or roll really well and be capable of putting the entire circle on the backfoot (barring the use of charms that can be activated after the roll has already taken place).<br /> <br /> I think my preference would be to borrow from the rules for Environmental Hazards because in practice I've found that if the players are rolling vs. a fixed difficulty it's more likely that a couple of them will fail despite having good dice pools on paper. There's some disadvantages to the fix, most notably the more I smooth out the irregularities the harder it becomes harder to translate the individual profile into a battle group profile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah your original problem seems like a good remark I never thought of before.<br /> <br /> Did you come to any solution ? I'm curious","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T07:06:50-07:00","id":1340942,"title":"","content":"I've still not got a good idea for translating the attack profile into an enviromental hazard beyond &quot;eyeball it and hope for the best&quot; but I'm hoping to test in soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T17:32:06-07:00","id":1341021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1338627#post1338627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-farming ini on one target and unleashing it on another being an optimal strat in many cases</div> </div> </div> </div>This has a very simple solution. The core book is explicit about initiative and withering attacks being an abstraction of gaining the upper hand in a fight. If a character tries to make a decisive attack against a different opponent than the one he's been fighting, he immediately resets to base initiative. Gaining advantage against Kingfisher Swift doesn't confer advantage against Harmonious Jade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T03:52:47-07:00","id":1341072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341021#post1341021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has a very simple solution. The core book is explicit about initiative and withering attacks being an abstraction of gaining the upper hand in a fight. If a character tries to make a decisive attack against a different opponent than the one he's been fighting, he immediately resets to base initiative. Gaining advantage against Kingfisher Swift doesn't confer advantage against Harmonious Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the explicit rule though. And there's plenty of in genre examples of a tense combat between two parties which unexpectedly culminates in the death of a third party. Especially if all three are in a swirling melee and Harmonious Jade is launching attacks against you which you're fending off. And what if you're alternating Withering attacks between the two? What if you're cutting a path through Swift to get to Jade as Jade peppers you with arrows you're swatting out of the sky as you inexorably push the Terrestrial back to get to your true target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T05:18:36-07:00","id":1341079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341072#post1341072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the explicit rule though. And there's plenty of in genre examples of a tense combat between two parties which unexpectedly culminates in the death of a third party.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is best handled narratively: &quot;But suddenly, as you thrust for Swift's heart, Sesus Eshuvar throws himself between you!&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially if all three are in a swirling melee and Harmonious Jade is launching attacks against you which you're fending off. </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that there's no mechanism for &quot;fending off&quot; attacks; Parry and Evasion are both static values.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what if you're alternating Withering attacks between the two? </div> </div> </div>You'd be resetting to base every time you switch targets; possibly avoidable with a Charm, but giving one foe a chance to catch her breath loses any advantage you'd accrued.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if you're cutting a path through Swift to get to Jade as Jade peppers you with arrows you're swatting out of the sky as you inexorably push the Terrestrial back to get to your true target? </div> </div> </div>You've got to put Swift out of the fight before you engage Jade; otherwise, Swift has a clear shot at your back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1856,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","user":"Hakkonen","date":". 10-13-2019, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T06:48:10-07:00","id":1341084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341021#post1341021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has a very simple solution. The core book is explicit about initiative and withering attacks being an abstraction of gaining the upper hand in a fight. If a character tries to make a decisive attack against a different opponent than the one he's been fighting, he immediately resets to base initiative. Gaining advantage against Kingfisher Swift doesn't confer advantage against Harmonious Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a bit too harsh-- and worse, I'd be concerned that it'll make combat more static. Like how attacks of opportunity in d&amp;d encourage you to just sit there trading blows, rather than maneuvering around the fight. A flat penalty might work though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T07:49:18-07:00","id":1341090,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no, that would solve nothing and create a hell of a lot of new problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T10:31:00-07:00","id":1341107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341079#post1341079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got to put Swift out of the fight before you engage Jade; otherwise, Swift has a clear shot at your back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cynis Ganan swings his jade tetsubo in punishing arcs, driving Kingfisher Swift back with every blow, jade ringing on jade -- but not on Jade, Ganan's true target.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why are you protecting this demon!&quot; Ganan bellows with the voice of an avalanche.<br /> <br /> Harmonious Jade looses another arrow, but Ganan twirls a hundred pounds of jade as if it where a swagger stick, knocking the arrow from its path.<br /> <br /> Swift tries to duck in under Ganan's guard, but can find no opening.<br /> <br /> Ganan swings again, this blow connects sending Swift reeling. She Crashes to the ground, clearly out-fought, and Ganan barrels past her, bringing his tetsubo to bear on the hated Anathema...<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Swift has a clear shot at your back when you reset to base <i>after</i> launching a Decisive against Jade. Resetting before the attack just means the blows you traded with Swift are worthless and the attack against Jade is weaker.<br /> <br /> And what does &quot;out of the fight&quot; even mean? Surely the closest thing to that is Crashing someone. If I have to kill one opponent before I can begin fighting the next, that's going to lead to a lot of kills...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T12:28:41-07:00","id":1341120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341079#post1341079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got to put Swift out of the fight before you engage Jade; otherwise, Swift has a clear shot at your back.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of does already happen, sort of. If you crash swift and then turn your attention to decisive attack Jade, Swift has a fantastic chance to wreck your shit.<br /> <br /> Like let\u2019s say you\u2019re battling Swift, force her down to -3 initiative, which gives you a big initiative break and shoots you up to 22i or something. Then you say \u201cah good now that I have all this initiative I can smash Jade.\u201d and then you turn around, leap to Jade and decisive, maybe killing her or forcing her to accept a crippling injury. Then you reset to 3i and it moves to Swifts turn.<br /> <br /> Well now you\u2019ve turned your back on the person you\u2019ve been battling this whole time, so she smashes into your back and deals 4 withering damage to you, which puts you at -1i. She gets 1i for hitting, 4i for her damage, and 5i for Initiative Break. Which puts her at 7i. Then because Initiative Shift, she gets to roll her Join Battle pool and add that to her initiative, so now she\u2019s at like 11i, then her turn immediately resets for that round, so she attacks you again, withering you for another 5 withering damage. Now you\u2019re at -6i with 2 onslaught penalties and she\u2019s at +17i. Then the round ends and she gets to go again because she\u2019s got the most initiative and she either decisives you with her decent amount of initiative, or takes the opportunity to hammer you further into the dirt in preparation for finishing you off.<br /> <br /> There are some times when that might be worth it, like if Jade is about to unleash some devastating attack that will kill you, but you definitely get punished for switching targets between gathering initiative and launching decisive attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T13:47:25-07:00","id":1341129,"title":"","content":"Yes, this situation is only a problem in my eyes if Kingfisher Swift has essentially already been beaten (scene-length penalties, no motes or way too far into negative initiative) but is being kept on her feet for entirely meta reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:20:26-07:00","id":1341139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341129#post1341129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this situation is only a problem in my eyes if Kingfisher Swift has essentially already been beaten (scene-length penalties, no motes or way too far into negative initiative) but is being kept on her feet for entirely meta reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually IS an explicit rule. Page 193 of the core \u201cIf the Storyteller decides that a Crashed character has no hope of recovery against his opponents, and that his continued presence will only serve to give the players a \u201cfree\u201d source of Initiative, she can declare the Crashed character defeated the next time he suffers a successful withering attack.\u201d<br /> <br /> If Kingfisher Swift is down and completely out, then the next time they\u2019re attacked they\u2019re removed. I will point out though that as an exalt it takes some serious work to put someone like Kingfisher in a position where they\u2019re just offering up free initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T16:36:24-07:00","id":1341169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341139#post1341139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That actually IS an explicit rule. Page 193 of the core \u201cIf the Storyteller decides that a Crashed character has no hope of recovery against his opponents, and that his continued presence will only serve to give the players a \u201cfree\u201d source of Initiative, she can declare the Crashed character defeated the next time he suffers a successful withering attack.\u201dIf Kingfisher Swift is down and completely out, then the next time they\u2019re attacked they\u2019re removed.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know. I playtested these rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I will point out though that as an exalt it takes some serious work to put someone like Kingfisher in a position where they\u2019re just offering up free initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of the tricky part. It is rare that an Exalt is going to be made weak enough to simply giving up free initiative but different Storytellers are going to draw the line differently on whats considered to be close enough that Kingfisher Swift remaining a part of this combat is disruptive and immersion breaking.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T05:35:34-07:00","id":1341239,"title":"","content":"Part of why I'm sympathetic to having a house rule for switching opponents is because I can see how this can causes issues with the group's social contract.<br /> <br /> Pulling Kingfisher Swift at the earliest opportunity might come across to the players as a veiled accusation of cheating, especially if they've got a way that this fight plays out in their mind that makes perfect sense to them. I can see how being locked into attacking one opponent at a time even in and punished for deviating from that, even in a 5 on 1 melee could serve as a path of least resistance if you know all too well what some people in your gaming group (including you) are like and want to avoid this misery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T13:05:52-07:00","id":1341690,"title":"","content":"One thing I've been trying to test for a little while but have been having issues with due to how my.plauers have resolved encounters or discussed what they want out of my game is splitting combats.<br /> <br /> For instance, say your Circle of 5 Ecalts engages 2 Exalts; a Dusk, a Daybreak, the Daybreak's undead Rhino Centaur bodyguard, and a group of Zombies.<br /> <br /> Rather then a massive pile of Initiatives, I'd prefer to split up to where, for instance, the Dawn and the Night engage the Dusk, the Zenith fights the Rhino Bodyguard, and the Twilight and Eclipse fight the Daybreak and the Zombies. <br /> <br /> In this idea, each of these would in effect be a miniature fight in itself; you can't 'cross over' fights; the Dawn can't smack the much weaker Daybreak to farm Initiative to kill the Dusk, and similarly the Dusk can't do that to the Eclipse; they have to stay focused on their own opponents or they risk opening themselves up for an attack.<br /> <br /> However, in addition to this would be special Disengage Gambits that use the same rules as Disengaging but rather then leaving the range, they instead 'Tag-Out' without another ally, swapping places with them in their fight, possibly getting a bonus to their next attack for doing so as a 'surprise' action.<br /> <br /> So for instance, the Dusk might call the Zombies to distract the Dawn and get a sneak attack on the Eclipse, or the Twilight might leave the zombies to the Eclipse to go join the Zenith in dealing with the monster.<br /> <br /> As each battle ended you slowly fold the combatants into other fights, or they stay out of the others if they're too exhausted or injured.<br /> <br /> Hopefully I get to try this relatively soon and get some notes on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T14:23:34-07:00","id":1341707,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the judicious use of Range Bands accomplish much the same thing? If the Zenith/Rhino duel is at Short Range to the Dawn/Night/Dusk melee, that separates things nicely-- if you try to repeatedly Disengage and switch between opponents, you're losing initiative for sure, and quite possibly an entire action. Due to the way Disengage works, it also sort of makes the &quot;stickiness&quot; of being in a duel relative to the strength of your opponent, which I think makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T14:46:55-07:00","id":1341711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341690#post1341690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've been trying to test for a little while but have been having issues with due to how my.plauers have resolved encounters or discussed what they want out of my game is splitting combats.<br /> <br /> For instance, say your Circle of 5 Ecalts engages 2 Exalts; a Dusk, a Daybreak, the Daybreak's undead Rhino Centaur bodyguard, and a group of Zombies.<br /> <br /> Rather then a massive pile of Initiatives, I'd prefer to split up to where, for instance, the Dawn and the Night engage the Dusk, the Zenith fights the Rhino Bodyguard, and the Twilight and Eclipse fight the Daybreak and the Zombies.<br /> <br /> In this idea, each of these would in effect be a miniature fight in itself; you can't 'cross over' fights; the Dawn can't smack the much weaker Daybreak to farm Initiative to kill the Dusk, and similarly the Dusk can't do that to the Eclipse; they have to stay focused on their own opponents or they risk opening themselves up for an attack.<br /> <br /> However, in addition to this would be special Disengage Gambits that use the same rules as Disengaging but rather then leaving the range, they instead 'Tag-Out' without another ally, swapping places with them in their fight, possibly getting a bonus to their next attack for doing so as a 'surprise' action.<br /> <br /> So for instance, the Dusk might call the Zombies to distract the Dawn and get a sneak attack on the Eclipse, or the Twilight might leave the zombies to the Eclipse to go join the Zenith in dealing with the monster.<br /> <br /> As each battle ended you slowly fold the combatants into other fights, or they stay out of the others if they're too exhausted or injured.<br /> <br /> Hopefully I get to try this relatively soon and get some notes on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds interesting. Separating combatants into separate duels does feel like a good fit for Exalted's cinematic approach to combat. The only problem would be when a character's skills reward team play, such as someone with Archery or Charms that buff or defend others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341707#post1341707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the judicious use of Range Bands accomplish much the same thing? If the Zenith/Rhino duel is at Short Range to the Dawn/Night/Dusk melee, that separates things nicely-- if you try to repeatedly Disengage and switch between opponents, you're losing initiative for sure, and quite possibly an entire action. Due to the way Disengage works, it also sort of makes the &quot;stickiness&quot; of being in a duel relative to the strength of your opponent, which I think makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main problem is when combatants have ranged attacks, which would allow them to &quot;cheat&quot;. Also there may be other impacts, for instance Charms that require you to win Join Battle might be easier to pull off since you're not rolling against the enemies in the other duels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T14:59:58-07:00","id":1341713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1341711#post1341711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds interesting. Separating combatants into separate duels does feel like a good fit for Exalted's cinematic approach to combat. The only problem would be when a character's skills reward team play, such as someone with Archery or Charms that buff or defend others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the main problem is when combatants have ranged attacks, which would allow them to &amp;quot;cheat&amp;quot;. Also there may be other impacts, for instance Charms that require you to win Join Battle might be easier to pull off since you're not rolling against the enemies in the other duels.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the first part, this is why such duels wouldn't be 1 on 1. The Zenith battle singer in such an idea would probably have a bodyguard trying to protect them from an enemy who is trying to cut off the advantage. <br /> <br /> Depending on how it's set up, for buffing charms like that or the Empowering Shout, I'd lean towards the idea of that charm being able to cross the 'borders' as it were, since they're just theoretical ones anyway; if you're playing the buffer person you're probably not actively attacking at the same time, meaning you're not upending the Initiative order.<br /> <br /> It could create a sort of battle where someone has to protect the 'strategist' while they buff the other combatants to be able to handle other foes.<br /> <br /> As for Range Bands, many abilities have the ability to swap into new range bands either with attacks or powers of charms. Range bands themselves often suffer from being just constricting and vague enough that players can have trouble keeping track of them, since all of them are relative to each other; the game doesn't support the idea of a central 'feature' to base range bands off of, so a lot of my players often miss or forget they're too far away to attack someone, or get confused on how they work in certain aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T02:49:29-07:00","id":1341825,"title":"","content":"I tested Flare's idea during my first campaign and it went very well I think, but there are few characteristics to be careful about :<br /> <br /> - It doesn't have to be 1v1 (just been said)<br /> <br /> - The actors of each fight need to have a special link between them that makes the fight more tense : My first fight was between a Twilight and his Lunar mate, the second was between the Night and an Abyssal that almost destroyed his soul in a prior scenario, and the last was the Dawn and Eclipse against the enemy Exigent and his troops, and the Solars had very strong empathic history between them (the Dawn ended killing the Eclipse after the fight because of a Limit Break, and they were the couple of characters with the most interesting dual link between them so it was very emotionnal). Due to this limitation, I don't advise using this method every time<br /> <br /> - Every fights needs to have clear objectives for the overall battle that are more than &quot;Win or loss&quot; : The Night was disabling a 2nd Circle Demon from the inside that made the enemy troops immortals; The Twilight and Lunar were fighting to end the Solar/lunar bond that tied them, and the Dawn and Eclipse were protecting the immaculate temple full of artifacts and emprisonned gods that could serve as weapons. If there are no &quot;direct consequences&quot; to the fight except hp loss it's not worth I think<br /> <br /> - I think it's best if it's setup and discussed with the players. Who do you want to fight ? At what objective ? Why ?<br /> <br /> Here were my 2 cents","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T23:38:41-07:00","id":1342479,"title":"","content":"I currently just use the house rule that a crashed character cannot provide any more initiative and is an invalid target for further withering attacks. Basically, the logic is that being in crash is a mechanical abstraction of a narratively appropriate moment for an impactful attack to connect and so gives plot armor against narratively inappropriate attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T00:57:45-07:00","id":1342488,"title":"","content":"This one is interesting really but how do you handle for example everyone being crashed ? Or one party being crashed and not the other ? I really like it because I feel like this idea can leave you to make a scene transition where a losing party is brought to its knee and surrender or flee without everyone losing too much hp","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T03:55:12-07:00","id":1342496,"title":"","content":"The main place I see that rule get broken is when it's the player characters vs. a battle group and their leader.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the battle group rolls well (or they're a Lunar with Invincible Beast Warrior Empowerment) and crashes all of the PCs<b>, </b>so for anyone who can't do enough damage to cause size loss and get the initative break bonus their only recourse for getting back into positive numbers before the battle group has a chance to attack their health level track is to make withering attacks against the only enemy character present. Ordinarily this would be time to step in but if they've masterminded the attack that just crashed everyone they're winning regardless of what the initiative track is showing.<br /> <br /> We once had this happen with the added complication of poison vs. a sorceress with a battle group of elementals. In terms of numbers we had her on the ropes but every time someone failed to connect with her they were being quickly overcome by either the poison or the battle group and when it was down to 1v1 the sorceress quickly got an initiative shift and proceeded to beat the shit out of our last remaining fighter.<br /> <br /> Still, it goes back to social contracts and knowing your group. Is my scenario more likely to happen or do you think it's more likely that you'll end up with one of the PCs spending 20 minutes kicking a defeated enemy around the room like a football, because they want to power up their finishing move and this is <i>clearly</i> how fighting works in this world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 10-20-2019, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T09:08:46-07:00","id":1342539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1342496#post1342496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main place I see that rule get broken is when it's the player characters vs. a battle group and their leader.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the battle group rolls well (or they're a Lunar with Invincible Beast Warrior Empowerment) and crashes all of the PCs<b>, </b>so for anyone who can't do enough damage to cause size loss and get the initative break bonus their only recourse for getting back into positive numbers before the battle group has a chance to attack their health level track is to make withering attacks against the only enemy character present. Ordinarily this would be time to step in but if they've masterminded the attack that just crashed everyone they're winning regardless of what the initiative track is showing.<br /> <br /> We once had this happen with the added complication of poison vs. a sorceress with a battle group of elementals. In terms of numbers we had her on the ropes but every time someone failed to connect with her they were being quickly overcome by either the poison or the battle group and when it was down to 1v1 the sorceress quickly got an initiative shift and proceeded to beat the shit out of our last remaining fighter.<br /> <br /> Still, it goes back to social contracts and knowing your group. Is my scenario more likely to happen or do you think it's more likely that you'll end up with one of the PCs spending 20 minutes kicking a defeated enemy around the room like a football, because they want to power up their finishing move and this is <i>clearly</i> how fighting works in this world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think if you use it strategically or for shenanigans it might be a bad idea. But other than that, there has been few times where the fight became dull and having a transition based on some mechanical indicator (people are crashed) might be a good indicator for it. It also emphasizes not everyone attacking the non-combatant to gain initiative because attacking the familiar Lyzard-tyrant is useless because of his ton of soak.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's perfect but it certainly has good points to it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T10:13:52-07:00","id":1345253,"title":"","content":"I ran through the first half of a combat using my idea of split combats in the same area last night in order to attempt to cut down the complexity of a combat involving 2 battle groups, 4 PC combatants, and 5 non-PC combatants.<br /> <br /> I split it into 2 PCs and an Ally NPC against 1 NPC and a Battle Group, and 2 PCs and a Battle group against 3 non-PC combatants.<br /> <br /> They all agreed that the fight was much less complicated and we got through rounds a good deal faster because the split combat allowed them to essentially cut down on their possible targets for combat and not worry about having to be ready to defend against huge amounts of opponents all at once, while still allowing a fight to appear as a chaotic mess of multiple goals all pushing against each other.<br /> <br /> Next week is going to be part two of the same fight, as the conditions have changed significantly, and we'll be testing a longer, more indepth fight instead of a 2 round brawl with the same concepts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:39:11-08:00","id":1346793,"title":"","content":"Some people in the thread about whining because there is not enough Exalted asked me my home-brew &quot;Quick NPC&quot; so I'll share it here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'll try to present it simply in 2 parts.<br /> <br /> First part : I think it can be useful for about everyone.<br /> <br /> This is essentially a sort of cheat sheet for scores of NPCs. I divided the power level of characters in basically 6, from mediocre to monstrous. Usually power level from 1 to 5 cover what a playable character can have, with level 6 being the strange NPC that have stats beyond what can be achieved with today's game mechanics. I do not claim it to be impartial or always perfectly representing the balance of the game, but usually NPC's from the books are within the appropriate descriptions of my home-brew. Each part is in 3 lines : The second line contains the topic covered and the associated score to each power level on the appropriate columns, the first line is examples of creatures that I see fit the scores given, and a black line separates the following topic. I'm pretty bad at designing cool beautiful files so don't judge me.<br /> <br /> I activated comments so if you want to make useful comments I can change the file. You can obviously just copy the file and change it at your own will.<br /> <br /> Second part : My personal addition to it<br /> <br /> Because I don't like handling essence 5 by 5 and having multiple different NPC's working under different core mechanics, I basically consider everything works like Solars because I ind their functioning simple, ie everyone can add dices to their pool in exchange for motes in a straightforward manner, and I divided essence pools by 5. Each &quot;Essence power&quot; one might use cost 1 Essence if the power is from mediocre to average, and 2 Essence if it's from Strong to Monstruous. This way, if on first round a very old Dragon blooded attacked with full Excellency (Average in Excellencies so cost 1 Essence), and used maximum Charms to add maximum damage because he is specialized in this (so +8 damage with essence, so cost 2 Essence), he used 3 Essence of his 14 pool of Essence. All Essence regenerate by 1 on each round. This basically handles all &quot;numeral&quot; Charms, that somehow gives you mostly dices bonus and small scenaristic power. You can of course use Charms that have more scenaristic effects, for 1 Essence for weaker Charms to 3 Essence to world-defining Charms. <br /> <br /> I believe the main weakness of this home-brew is that I didn't add enough examples to it, so I can use it quite fairly with my experience, but really new ST might be confused and use power level very far from the intended power level expected by the game, but it might get a little better if I get some comments to help me. <br /> <br /> Also there might be some French because I didn't check everything, but I think almost everything is English understandable. Do not hesitate to ask questions if you have some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T14:23:55-08:00","id":1346853,"title":"","content":"So if I'm understanding this right, what you've got is essentially a series of benchmarks. A trained professional should have a dice pool in the field of around 6. An anti-Dawn Caste Abyssal should have Parry/Evade around 6. A huge elemental should have a Soak of around 16 (12+4). Which is... really helpful, thank you.<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure I follow how you're handling magic type stuff. I see that you're cutting Essence scaling down, so that an Essence 3 Abyssal might have 12 Essence and Charms costing 1-2 point each, which is sensible enough. And I see you're simplifying die tricks Charms to all work roughly like Solar Excellencies, which is a reasonable simplification. I'm not sure how you get from that to the actual number of dice rolled, though-- could you explain a little more? Perhaps give an example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:10:21-08:00","id":1346865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1346853#post1346853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I'm understanding this right, what you've got is essentially a series of benchmarks. A trained professional should have a dice pool in the field of around 6. An anti-Dawn Caste Abyssal should have Parry/Evade around 6. A huge elemental should have a Soak of around 16 (12+4). Which is... really helpful, thank you.<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure I follow how you're handling magic type stuff. I see that you're cutting Essence scaling down, so that an Essence 3 Abyssal might have 12 Essence and Charms costing 1-2 point each, which is sensible enough. And I see you're simplifying die tricks Charms to all work roughly like Solar Excellencies, which is a reasonable simplification. I'm not sure how you get from that to the actual number of dice rolled, though-- could you explain a little more? Perhaps give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure thanks for your questions I will try to explain. <br /> <br /> There are 2 different types of lines, but this is not noted anywhere except in my mind so I guess for other people it's not crystal clear. <br /> <br /> There are the lines that are &quot;plain basic stats&quot; : Comp\u00e9tence, Pr\u00e9cision d'attaque, Malus, D\u00e9gats, Points de vie, D\u00e9fense (Statique) and Soak/Hardness. They are very straightforward : Any character corresponding the description should have these stats. So indeed, an anti-Dawn Caste Abyssal should have Parry/Evade around 6, and a Huge elemental should have Soak around 12 (Note the 12, I will explain why not 16). I think these lines are useful for everyone because they mainly respect what's written in Core Books and are pretty accurate, everyone can use them and they don't have really any &quot;houserule&quot;.<br /> <br /> Then there are the lines that use Essence or are affected by it : Pool d'essence, Excellencies, Double et reroll, and Bonus soak/damage. As I said previously, I basically took every effect and costs from the Core Books, divided them by 5, averaged them, and made the one that are purely &quot;numeric&quot; work like Solar Excellencies. So for example, huge Elementals will generally have a Soak of 12. Suppose the elemental has a little of spiritual power, so they have an essence pool of 14. When this elemental defends against an attack, he will first use an Excellency to defend himself, and raise his Parry of 4 (Line : Defense (statique), he's huge and used to fight, but maybe not very agile) to 6 (Line : Excellencies (succ\u00e8s), elementals are usually not potent to add lots of successes). For that, he used 1 Essence, passing him to 13. He get hit, so now he soaks with his 12 soak (Line : Soak/Hardness), and he can use 1 essence to raise his soak by 4 to 16 (Line : Bonus soak/damage d'essence, he is an elemental of battle), putting his Essence to 12. He might have a special elemental power that create a puddle of elemental power when damaged and put difficult terrain around him or environmental damage for ennemies that stay around. I'd rate it a pretty powerful power, so it certainly costs 2 Essence, putting him at 10 Essence. Next turn, he will regain 1 Essence making him begin the turn at 11 Essence. (I think Essence is gained at the beginning of the turn but I'm not sure I admit).<br /> <br /> Does that help ? The last line with scores &quot;Bonus soak/damage d'essence&quot; might not be clear to other people than me because of the formulation, but it means that on average a character with Charms will obtain the corresponding bonus through use of Essence.<br /> <br /> For the rest you described pretty well what I did. For example, the Abyssal Essence 3 has 12 Essence on my home-brew, which makes 12*5 = 70, which approximates his real 66 motes of Essence. For rolling dices, you take the appropriate pool and roll it. I took the habit of just rolling basic dices pool, and considering every excellency to be direct Charm success in order to spend less time counting dices (Line : Excellencies), but you can also just double the number given on this line and use them as Charmed dices to roll instead of Charm Successes. So for example, the Abyssal with a huge weapon will certainly be around 10 dices to attack, and spending 2 of his 12 Essence, he can gain 5 successes (or 10 bonus dices to roll) on his attack.<br /> <br /> I think that pretty much cover it. I'm still open for questions if things stay unclear. I think my home-brew should really just be considered a detailed and compulsed chart of NPCs and mechanics that are in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T06:12:33-08:00","id":1347666,"title":"","content":"Over in another thread, I was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347521#post1347521\">discussing some of the ways </a>to make non-supernatural foes in Exalted be plausible threats to Solar Exalted in combat. While I was writing that post, though, a couple of things occurred to me that I find a bit unsatisfying with battlegroups as they're currently handled. These house rules are attempts to address those issues.<br /> <br /> First, while battlegroups do get a bit of a bonus to hit, which can get <i>quite</i> nice if a commander gives them appropriate orders, it's all in the form of a bonus, and doesn't engage the existing way the system uses to handle being &quot;swarmed&quot; - namely, onslaught penalties. If you attack a Solar Melee specialist with five individual mortal soldiers, the last one will actually stand a chance of hitting her, or at the very least, make her spend more motes on things like Bulwark Stance. If you group the same five individuals into a battlegroup, however, they get just +1 to hit once, and the Invincible Sword Princess barely has to strain to improve her Parry. That seems off, to me - battlegroups are supposed to be a time-saver for the ST, not something that critically nerfs the opponents they want to throw, and the PC's charms shouldn't be rendered pointless quite so frequently.<br /> <br /> So, my proposed houserule: when a battlegroup attacks an individual, it automatically imposed an onslaught penalty on the target's Defense, equal to the battlegroup's Size. This penalty applies to the target's Defense against the battlegroup's attack, and then stays until the target's turn, as normal for onslaught penalties. Battlegroups can still attack multiple targets, but if they attack multiple targets who are all within Close range of each other, they must divide the onslaught penalty between the targets, rounding down. For instance, if a Size 4 battlegroup of hobgoblins attacks Volfer, Prince Diamond, and Novia Claro, and Volfer and Diamond are within Close range of each other, the onslaught penalty suffered by Volfer and Diamond would only be -2 each, while Novia would suffer the full -4. This is intended to encourage PCs to stay together in fights, and pull stunts like back-to-back fighting and stuff like that.<br /> <br /> The second, more minor issue that I'm not really satisfied with how the movement rules handle one character, or a group of them, trying to get past another character - the classic &quot;one warrior bravely guarding the narrow way so that others can escape&quot; scenario. As it stands, someone trying to pass by is doing a disengage, which is always (Dexterity+Dodge), and the opposing character must roll (Dexterity+Athletics). This devalues fighting skill in the &quot;hold the line&quot; scenario, which is, I would argue, an important element. When the Spartans hold the Persian army back at the battle of Thermopylae, it's not their raw strength or skill at athletic pursuit that matters, it's their skill with their <i>weapons</i>.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I'd introduce a new combat action, &quot;Hold the Line&quot;. This costs 2 initiative, and it places the character who takes it in the path of anyone trying to move past them. Anyone who attempts to move past them through their Close range band must make an opposed roll against the fighter barring their way. The character holding the line rolls (Dexterity+[Brawl or Melee]), depending on how they're fighting, while the person trying to move past them rolls (Dexterity + [Brawl, Dodge, or Melee]). If the fighter holding the line wins the roll, they also inflict withering damage on the opponent equal to their margin of victory, and the opponent can't get past them. If the opponent wins, they move past. A character holding the line can't take other combat movement actions, including their reflexive movement, without abandoning the attempt to block passage, and they can't oppose disengage attempts by the opponent if the opponent isn't trying to disengage past the spot they are guarding. Battlegroups gain a bonus equal to their Size on all contested rolls involved in holding the line, whether attempting it or trying to pass. Additionally, poor Drill gives -2 to such rolls, while Elite Drill gives +2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T06:42:51-08:00","id":1347672,"title":"","content":"I like a lot your ideas I'm trying to think about their possible consequences but I really think I might add them to my campaigns, to some extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T06:50:30-08:00","id":1347673,"title":"","content":"Would the onslaught penalty replace the usual bonus to attack, or would they stack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T07:49:53-08:00","id":1347680,"title":"","content":"I think they stack, presented as it it, which is kinda very strong. Maybe the onslaught should only be applied after the attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T09:38:45-08:00","id":1347702,"title":"","content":"I like those houserules a lot, although I think I'd just fold Hold the Line into the Full Defense action, for both flavor and simplicity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T12:26:47-08:00","id":1347734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1347702#post1347702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like those houserules a lot, although I think I'd just fold Hold the Line into the Full Defense action, for both flavor and simplicity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really good. Not only does it aid simplicity, it makes the Full Defense action worth using (or at least more worth it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T13:02:08-08:00","id":1347741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1347673#post1347673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the onslaught penalty replace the usual bonus to attack, or would they stack?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1347680#post1347680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they stack, presented as it it, which is kinda very strong. Maybe the onslaught should only be applied after the attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intent was that both the onslaught penalty and and the normal bonus for Size would apply. I don't like the onslaught penalty only applying after the attack, because it still means that a battlegroup on its own is probably not going to hit, since the onslaught penalty will usually go away before they get a chance to attack again. The combination does make battlegroups overall more powerful, but I'm pretty much okay with that result - while large battlegroups are currently dangerous, small ones, I find, tend to be less dangerous than if you just ran the combatants individually, and I think this compensates for that. <br /> <br /> That said, if you don't want to make battlegroups overall more powerful, dropping the bonus to hit from Size would probably be the most logical. That would, however, mean that if a Size 5 battlegroup attacked 6 or more characters in Close range of one another, their numbers would provide absolutely no benefit, which also seems off. Perhaps as a compromise, subtract the onslaught penalty being inflicted from the battlegroup's bonus to attack from Size? That makes the calculation a bit more complex, of course, but not cripplingly so, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T13:06:42-08:00","id":1347744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1347702#post1347702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like those houserules a lot, although I think I'd just fold Hold the Line into the Full Defense action, for both flavor and simplicity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's certainly a thought, though I worry that if there's no mechanic for the person holding the line to gain initiative, they'll eventually get crashed and fail anyway. Was the intent that it would still be the mechanics as I presented them (i.e. the person holding the line gets init if they win the contest), it's just called Full Defense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T13:11:28-08:00","id":1347746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1347744#post1347744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's certainly a thought, though I worry that if there's no mechanic for the person holding the line to gain initiative, they'll eventually get crashed and fail anyway. Was the intent that it would still be the mechanics as I presented them (i.e. the person holding the line gets init if they win the contest), it's just called Full Defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, basically Hold the Line would become a bonus perk you get (with the opportunity to gain ini and all) if someone tries to move through you while you use Full Defense.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit :</i> I would also be tempted to make Hold the line cause an actual Withering Clash between the contestants rather than a special opposed roll, although that's more of a personal preference, the opposed roll is probably a safer bet balance-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 11-11-2019, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T13:34:00-08:00","id":1347752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics?p=1347746#post1347746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Edit :</i> I would also be tempted to make Hold the line cause an actual Withering Clash between the contestants rather than a special opposed roll, although that's more of a personal preference, the opposed roll is probably a safer bet balance-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered just making it a clash, but decided against it for a couple of reasons. First, clashes are already pretty potent - being able to use your combat skill against the enemy, instead of your Defense, when your weapon skill isn't affected by onslaught penalties or other defense-only modifiers, and when it's probably your best pool anyway, is quite good. Adding the ability to prevent enemy movement on <i>top</i> of that just seemed overpowered. Second, I think that making this mechanically distinct from a clash opens up some interesting potential charm design space. I wouldn't mind seeing a few Solar Melee charms devoted to the idea of being an immovable object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T14:14:24-08:00","id":1347762,"title":"","content":"So Kelly Pedersen, you writing a new move has inspired me, and since there is another topic where I posted about my difficulties balancing &quot;intermediate&quot; encounters to make them interesting, I decided to write down some ideas that came to my mind.<br /> <br /> Here is the link to the document I just wrote.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12AIsDCFk7uZnbiBz1Y09oaOlwbyDbGVwkHVoB0SHGkg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Please, do not hesitate to make suggestions of you had the patience to read the whole of it. I must also excuse my English, I know I don't do too many grammar mistakes but my writing does not feel very English because of my native language and this is quite a long document.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to add some clarification : <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This may not appear clearly, but one purpose of these rules is to allow not for Fight Scenes only to have more tools that the ST can use, but rather to allow for making more easily engaging Action scenes where multiple interesting stakes can happen at once and ask for the players to come with creative solutions and unexpected development, which I feel is lacking in the action scenes at the moment in the game, because the ST has to invent all of them and be very inventive all the time without written support that facilitates his decisions.</span></span><br /> <br /> Here is its content, as of tonight :<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Introduction</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, your players decided to do something you didn\u2019t prepare for (the usual), and you thus have no idea what to do. You foolishly said that there is certainly a quite powerful god/kingdom/exigent west of here, and suddenly you find yourself saying \u201cHere you arrive at the gate of the palace/temple, and you see the guards and commanders preparing to fight you because reasons\u201d. But deep down, you know you got no NPCs prepared and no idea on how to handle what\u2019s next, but you do know that what\u2019s going to happen is all your NPC\u2019s are going to get crashed or dead, with no opportunity to do anything interesting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes it\u2019s fine, because your characters are so much stronger than anything else, and you don\u2019t really care about it, and you want it to go quick. But sometimes you are frustrated and you would have liked this to be at least interesting or challenging, even if ultimately you know your PCs are going to win, but you don\u2019t know how to do this. The purpose of this homebrew is to help you achieve this.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What this homebrew must achieve :</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Simplicity : It must not add complicated things to keep track of for the ST, who is certainly in this situation because he has already lots of work or few guidelines</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Abstraction : It must add tools that can be easily abstracted and re-used for the ST in different situation to add a variety of content</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fun : It must produce scenes or situations that the ST and players had fun participating</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Coherence : It must allow the ST and the players to play their characters in a way that seems in line with the rest of the mechanics and fluff of the game</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What this homebrew is not intended for :</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fighting some random thugs no one has any interest in. Just roll (Attribute + Ability) and be done with it.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Not resolve any final big battle against extremely powerful adversaries. Some ideas here might be useful for this kind of battle, but it\u2019s not its primary purpose.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">A way to cheat out the existing mechanics of the game. If any point in this homebrew can be used for shenanigans not present in the Core books, you should prioritize using the Core rules.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Balance. The purpose of this guide is to artificially help you raise the stakes of certain scenes. It will propose solutions that are not balanced, and you should not consider to use them in other places.</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TL;DR</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To sum it up, the purpose of this homebrew is to give easy access tool for STs who didn\u2019t have time to prepare encounters for NPCs they think should be meaningful or impressive, but do not know how to achieve it in a reasonable time of preparation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The actual content</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These rules are explicitly designed to be used only for the NPCs and the STs. Let the players use them for their party at your own risk.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Set-up and join battle </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the beginning of the encounter, chose a Flagbearer. The Flagbearer is usually the antagonist NPC who is in charge where the PCs are intervening and will oppose them, controlling the armies, directing lieutenants, wielding authority from his Evil Master etc \u2026 He will usually be Exalted, or supernaturally powerful in some way, but you didn\u2019t have enough time to flesh it out. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Flagbearer starts the fight rolling his usual initiative, and add another 5. So he rolls Join Battle with (Wits + Awareness) + 3 (Rules from the Core) + 5. The Flagbearer first action CANNOT be a decisive attack, else he forfeits 5 initiative. The Flagbearer then generates 3 initiative per round. This initiative is meant to be used by the Flagbearer to create dramatic circumstances that will create fun situations for the players to resolve. Trying to shenanigan this initiative in order to just do mass decisive damage to the PCs should be considered an act of bad faith, and you should be ashamed of it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Putting down the Flagbearer in some way is usually the objective of the PCs, and the fight should be considered almost done when this is achieved, except if another rule explicitly says so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TL;DR </span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Set your most important NPC as a Flagbearer, roll his initiative, and add another 5. Don\u2019t start with a decisive attack with him. The Flagbearer gains 3 initiative on each subsequent round for free. If the Flagbearer is beaten, the fight should usually end.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Charms</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>But</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> : Many Charms will involve your Flagbearer or its allies doing something, and your PCs will often react saying \u201cBut my elemental is supposed to be blocking the pathway with his powers\u201d or something along those lines. Whenever a Charm has this keyword, the player with the most interesting argument gain Initiative, from 1 if his argument is not very strong to 5 if his argument is very strong (Basically, the cost of the merit usually associated is a good scale). Can be gained only once per use of the Charm. This should act as a reward for the player when he doesn\u2019t already mechanically benefit from his resource, not a way for him to benefit from something already mechanically useful.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forward, guards !</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost : 3i.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type : Supplemental. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword : But</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Flagbearer designates a place that is at least at Medium (Long would be better) Range, and holds some sort of strategic, symbolic or magical importance. While travelling toward this place, the Flagbearer (and him alone) gains +3 soak and 2 Hardness per unit and per size of battlegroup accompanying him (ie being in Close Range or making sense to accompany him or protecting him through the use of some magical powers). For example, if he had a Battlegroup of Size 3 and a familiar with him, he would gain 12 soak and 8 Hardness). Should the road toward the objective be blocked definitively (like really definitively), the effect of this Charms end.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Charm can be used when Join Battle is rolled.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notes</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The evident purpose of this Charm is to help the ST protect the Flagbearer while he attains a place that hold scenaristical importance, like the temple of a friendly god that owes a debt to him, or secret room filled with traps that will protect him. It also prevents the players going full stupid on their main target and force them to confront the other forces present. It also can make for some interesting way the players can try to block the enemy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This shall not fall into their hands, flee !</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost : 3i</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type : Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword : But.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Flagbearer designates a close NPC or bystander that somehow recognizes his authority, set his initiative to the lowest of (his own initiative or 15), and entrust him with whatever MacGuffin (or keys of the safe, or the plans leading to the object) the players were looking for. The NPC, now called the Runner, then start to flee on its turn, gaining the following advantage :</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">If using combat movement, the Runner first reflexively moves a range band that doesn\u2019t count as his move action for the round (Illustrate with the Flagbearer\u2019s powers giving him some boost)</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">If not using combat movement, the Runner starts with 5 successes on anyone else trying to contest him (Illustrate with the Flagbearer\u2019s powers giving him some boost)</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">If the Runner was nameless, his pools for running are set as those of a professional runner : He rolls 7 dices for most athletical challenge for escaping. </span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Flagbearer or any close lieutenant close to him can help the Runner escape by reflexively spending 3 initiative to double his next roll. Do not abuse it, it\u2019s meant to make things more cool and tensed by illustrating cool powers of the NPCs when player characters are closing on the Runner and give them a challenge, not a free easy escape for the Runner with the object the players are desperately needing.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Runner cannot use a decisive attack while running away, except if he is totally cornered and has absolutely no way to escape. If he is a non combattant, he shouldn\u2019t be allowed to make a decisive attack at all. Should the Runner use a decisive attack, he loses the control of the Macguffin, that ideally goes close to the nearest precipice or equivalent.</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notes</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The evident purpose of this Charm is to give some sort of chase scene, and allows the athletics characters a chance to illustrate themselves by doing a dynamic chase. It also allows to illustrate the coolness and flexibility of the antagonist NPCs by finding imaginative ways his powers and armies can interact in a chase scene. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Do not use this Charm if the players have no way to chase someone, except if you consider they have failed to catch the Macguffin for long enough and deserve to lose its immediate track.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You think you can come past my armies ?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost : 3i</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type : Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword : But.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Flagbearer does not fight alone, and he will not be the first to fall. Upon being attacked, he can reflexively be the target of a Defend Other action for this attack by any close battlegroup he commands or any fidel lieutenant close to him. Only usable once for each lieutenant and each battle group size. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Should the attacking character still successfully hit him through the Defending character, the ST can decide to exceptionally protect the Flagbearer but at a great cost : </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">On a decisive attack, the Defending Character that intercepts the blow takes double damage (as if by Thunderbolt Attack Prana, but not cumulable with it).</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">On a withering attack, the attacking character can choose any ally in the fight. This ally will gain the same amount of initiative he does after successfully resolving the attack against the Flagbearer, but the Flagbearer does not lose any initiative as a direct result of the attack. </span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Will you stop me, or save the children ?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost : 5i</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type : Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword : But.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The luck every villain gets when the hero finally close on him. The Flagbearer designates something a PC care for deeply or has a positive intimacy toward. The designated object or person find itself in a terrible situation, usually through the confusion of the fight : the close walls start crumbling around it and threaten to smash it, a close magical relic activates and starts contaminating it with Wyld influence or Strange powers, a group of innocent bystanders get thrown in the middle of the confusion need protection else their fate sealed, etc \u2026</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notes</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The evident purpose of this Charm is to divert a PC that has a lethal opportunity on the Flagbearer or an important lieutenant using the famous trope of \u201cWhat is the most important to you ?\u201d, and allows the PC to illustrate himself with cool powers to save the day : Maybe he can Occult away the magic relic, use a Charm to stop the Wyld influence or bump the innocent victim out of harm\u2019s way. This Charm does not need the bad guy to know the intimacy of the PC : To him, it\u2019s just a fortunate turn of event.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are forces in this world that are beyond your comprehension !</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost : 10i</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type : Simple. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword : But.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When in a place of power (eg the heart of a manse) or theatrically impressing, the Flagbearer reveals he prepared for this day since a long time ago. Bound by a sworn pact, a promise of power, or a costly purchase, a huge figure comes to aid the Flagbearer, called the Titan. The Titan should be in the theme of where the action is taking place, and the one summoning it. The Titan emerges at close or short range from the Flagbearer, with 10 initiative. He does not act that turn, but is considered having used a Protect Other action on the Flagbearer that lasts until his next turn. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">His stats should include the following parameters : </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Titan is usually legendary size, with the associated benefits</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Titan health points should average (4*Number of PC units actively fighting)</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Titan will rarely fight to death, but should the players utterly defeat him, they should earn some sort of advantage for doing so (A god rival of the one defeated will contact them and give them a reward, the beating heart of an elemental is a precious magical component the players were looking for, etc \u2026 Do not hesitate to make use of State a Fact to earn the reward by one of the players to highlight them)</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Titan\u2019s attack and damage stats should threaten at least one fighting player (ie : Attack is (Defense of one player)*2 and Base damage is (Soak of a player +3))</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Titan\u2019s soak should not be higher that the base damage of the strongest player character in the group</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Titan CANNOT kill any player character not their very close ally, but he can greatly injure them. Anyone put down to 0 hp by The Titan can usually be stabilized by a medicine roll that takes into account the situation the players are in.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Titan is usually slow, constrained, or very proud. Upon crashing or defeating 1-3 player controlled units (1 if there are few, 3 if there are a lot of them), The Titan consider its job done, and will usually start leaving without demanding its rest, making it expressely clear to the players that he is no longer a threat and should not be pursued if they are in a bad shape.</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notes</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The evident purpose of this Charm is to surprise the players with some cool huge stuff to kill or confront, and give a chance for the Big Game Hunter players to illustrate himself. Do not use this Charm if the players are in a bad shape already. I implemented some safeguards so he doesn\u2019t become stupidly too lethal if for some reason mistakes were made.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Personal notes</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Here is my non exhaustive list of personal notes, advices and things I would like to upgrade.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Notes </span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Many of the ideas I have are certainly inspirations from recent games like DD that gives epic monsters special moves in their lairs, as well as the last post from Kelly Pedersen about making a new move</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">I am really open for criticism. Really. But don\u2019t come to explain to me that Exalted is already fine as it is, because that\u2019s not really the point of this homebrew.<br /> The &quot;But&quot; Keyword idea came to my mind when speaking to DrLoveMonkey in another thread about not using the retainers/allies of your PCs when they were important for a fight but not enough to actually include them in the mechanics of the fight, so you just put them in the background. I think it's a not too bad solution to use them in a satisfactory way</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Advices </span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Don\u2019t use it when you have an encounter you think is already balanced</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">Don\u2019t abuse it. Don\u2019t let your players abuse it.</span></li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Things I would like to upgrade</span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\">I\u2019d certainly add a Charm about improving a lieutenant in some form or another</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\">I\u2019d certainly add a Charm about passing the Flagbearer title to someone if the current one became irrelevant</span></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":".  Made my intentions clearer 11-11-2019, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}